.TH VMG 1 "2026" "vm-manager-gui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vmg \- window for the vm virtual machine manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vmg
[\fB\-\-no\-indicator\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vmg
shows the machines and images that
.BR vm (1)
manages, and does what its commands do.
.B vm gui
opens it too.
.PP
The sidebar lists this host, its machines and the images it holds. Selecting
one opens a tab. The host tab lists the machines and every image the
catalogues name in tables, with toggles that narrow them to running machines, held images or the
host's architecture, and a menu that acts on the checked rows. A machine's tab
shows its state, access, hardware, ports and volumes, and the actions its state
allows. An image's tab shows what
.B vm inspect
reports. Right-clicking a table row offers the same actions.
.PP
Consoles, shells, logs and file copies open as terminal tabs. A console tab is
attached to the machine's serial console; a shell tab runs
.BR ssh ;
a log tab follows the console log, whole or by its last lines.
.PP
The listing refreshes every two seconds and after every action. Progress is
shown at the foot of the window; outcomes and errors appear as toasts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-indicator
Do not publish a panel indicator. Closing the window then quits.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH ACTIONS
Each action corresponds to a
.B vm
command.
.TP
Run…, Import…, Update Catalogues, Prune…, Configuration
.BR run ", " import ", " update ", " prune " and " config .
Prune lists what a dry run finds before removing it.
.TP
Start, Settings…, Eject CD-ROM
.BR start ,
with its options in the settings dialog and
.BR \-\-eject .
.TP
Pause, Resume, Stop, Kill, Remove…
.BR pause ", " resume ", " stop ", " kill " and " rm .
.TP
Console, Shell, Logs, Copy Files…, Screen, Screenshot…, Clone…
.BR console ", " ssh ", " logs ", " cp ", " screen ", " screenshot " and " clone .
.TP
Pull, Export…, Remove…
.BR pull ", " export " and " rmi .
.SH THE INDICATOR
The indicator is a
.IR StatusNotifierItem ,
which KDE, Xfce, Cinnamon and MATE show. GNOME needs the
.B gnome\-shell\-extension\-appindicator
package. While an indicator is shown, closing the window hides it; the
indicator lists the machines and reopens the window.
.SH SETTINGS
The window's size, the sidebar's width and visibility, the table filters and
column widths are kept in GSettings under
.BR com.paperstack.VmManager .
.SH FILES
The same as
.BR vm (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vm (1),
.BR vm\-config (5)
